<Layout title="Scavland System Requirements & PC Download Specs (Scavland Game / Steam Deck)" description="Minimum and recommended PC system requirements for Scavland, official Steam download specs, controller support, and handheld settings." keywords="Scavland system requirements, Scavland download, download Scavland, Scavland PC download, Scavland game, Scav Lands, Scavland PC specs, Scavland Steam Deck, Scavland controller support, minimum specs" canonical="/system-requirements/">
  <article class="article-shell">
    <header class="article-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Hardware Specifications · Updated October 2026 (Update 0.8.0 / Hotfix 0.8.8)</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">System Requirements &amp; Download Specs</h1>
      <p class="lede">Complete technical specifications required to download and run Scavland smoothly on PC, plus Steam Deck and controller optimization notes.</p>
      <span class="evidence">Evidence: Official Steam store page &amp; announcements · Update 0.8.0 / Hotfix 0.8.8</span>
    </header>

    <div class="article-layout">
      <div class="article-content">
        <h2 id="specs">Official PC Hardware Requirements</h2>

        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));gap:16px;margin:20px 0;">
          <div style="background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);padding:20px;border-radius:4px;">
            <h3 style="margin-top:0;color:var(--acid);font:700 1.4rem 'Barlow Condensed';text-transform:uppercase;">Minimum Requirements</h3>
            <ul style="padding-left:18px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--ink);margin:0;font-size:0.88rem;">
              <li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10 64-bit</li>
              <li><strong>CPU:</strong> Intel Core i3-4160 / AMD FX-6300</li>
              <li><strong>RAM:</strong> 4 GB Memory</li>
              <li><strong>GPU:</strong> GTX 750 Ti / Radeon R7 260X (2 GB)</li>
              <li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 11</li>
              <li><strong>Storage:</strong> 4 GB available SSD/HDD</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div style="background:var(--panel);border:1px solid #3f5c42;padding:20px;border-radius:4px;">
            <h3 style="margin-top:0;color:var(--acid);font:700 1.4rem 'Barlow Condensed';text-transform:uppercase;">Recommended Requirements</h3>
            <ul style="padding-left:18px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--ink);margin:0;font-size:0.88rem;">
              <li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10 / 11 64-bit</li>
              <li><strong>CPU:</strong> Intel Core i5-6600K / Ryzen 5 1600</li>
              <li><strong>RAM:</strong> 8 GB Memory</li>
              <li><strong>GPU:</strong> GTX 1060 (6 GB) / Radeon RX 580 (8 GB)</li>
              <li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 11 / 12</li>
              <li><strong>Storage:</strong> 6 GB SSD (Recommended for fast loading)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 id="download">PC Download &amp; Steam Client Installation</h2>
        <p>
          Scavland is officially distributed on PC via <strong>Steam Early Access (App ID 3373500)</strong>. Downloading the game through the official Steam client ensures automatic installation of all updates (including Update 0.8.0 and Hotfix 0.8.8), cloud saves, and verified malware-free installation. The game requires approximately 4 GB to 6 GB of available storage space. For the complete Steam store overview—including pricing, Steam Deck performance notes, and feature list—see our <a href="/steam/" style="color:var(--acid,#b9e86c);font-weight:600;text-decoration:underline;">Scavland Steam Store Hub</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="deck">Steam Deck &amp; Handheld Compatibility (Update 0.7.0 / 0.8.0)</h2>
        <p>While Scavland is fundamentally built on lightweight 2D pixel physics, Early Access player reports and creator feedback note that handheld performance is optimized for 60 FPS:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Performance:</strong> Stable 60 FPS is easily achievable on standard Steam Deck and portable gaming handhelds.</li>
          <li><strong>Battery Performance:</strong> Estimated 4.5+ hours of continuous wasteland exploration on a single charge.</li>
          <li><strong>UI &amp; Font Scaling:</strong> Update 0.7.0 refined text sizing on 7-inch displays and added full gamepad support to the rebuilt Death Screen.</li>
          <li><strong>Controls:</strong> Full controller support is present, with customizable layout rebinding.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;font-size:0.92rem;color:var(--text-muted,#aaa);">
          For optimized TDP power profiles, verified 60 FPS settings, and recommended community controller layouts, see our dedicated <a href="/guide/scavland-steam-deck-and-handheld-settings/" style="color:var(--acid,#b9e86c);font-weight:600;text-decoration:underline;">Scavland Steam Deck &amp; Handheld Settings Guide</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="article-media">
          <img src="/images/screenshots/steam_ss_05.webp" alt="Scavland inventory and item management interface" />
          <p class="caption">High-contrast inventory grid and item inspection interface designed for 1080p and handheld screens</p>
        </div>

        <h2 id="macos">macOS &amp; Apple Silicon Status</h2>
        <div style="background:var(--panel);border-left:3px solid var(--acid);padding:16px 20px;margin:20px 0;border-radius:0 4px 4px 0;">
          <strong style="color:var(--acid);font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:0.85rem;text-transform:uppercase;display:block;margin-bottom:6px;">
            Official Developer Status: Pending Apple Approval
          </strong>
          <p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--ink);">
            Following intense community inquiries on Steam, developer NoShadow confirmed that the native macOS build of Scavland is code-complete and currently undergoing final Apple notarization and store review.
          </p>
          <ul style="margin:0;padding-left:18px;font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;">
            <li><strong>Supported Architecture:</strong> Full compatibility with Apple Silicon (M1, M2, M3, M4) and Intel-based MacBooks/iMacs.</li>
            <li><strong>Performance Target:</strong> Solid 60 FPS at native Retina resolutions with minimal battery draw.</li>
            <li><strong>Expected Availability:</strong> Will be unlocked on Steam as a free platform update for all Early Access owners once approved.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2 id="controls">Controller &amp; Mouse/Keyboard Support</h2>
        <p>Full gamepad support is natively supported with twin-stick aiming and customizable button layouts. Mouse &amp; keyboard precision remains fully supported for pixel-accurate sniping across the Mist.</p>

